{
    "chapter_num": 20,
    "verses_count": 8,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Siege and Capture of Rabbah"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "In the spring of the year, the time when kings go forth to battle, Jo′ab led out the army, and ravaged the country of the Ammonites, and came and besieged Rabbah. But David remained at Jerusalem. And Jo′ab smote Rabbah, and overthrew it. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And David took the crown of their king"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or Milcom See 1 Kings 11.5"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " from his head; he found that it weighed a talent of gold, and in it was a precious stone; and it was placed on David’s head. And he brought forth the spoil of the city, a very great amount. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he brought forth the people who were in it, and set them to labor"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Compare 2 Sam 12.31: Heb he sawed"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " with saws and iron picks and axes;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Compare 2 Sam 12.31: Heb saws"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and thus David did to all the cities of the Ammonites. Then David and all the people returned to Jerusalem."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Exploits against the Philistines"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And after this there arose war with the Philistines at Gezer; then Sib′becai the Hu′shathite slew Sip′pai, who was one of the descendants of the giants; and the Philistines were subdued. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And there was again war with the Philistines; and Elha′nan the son of Ja′ir slew Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the shaft of whose spear was like a weaver’s beam. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And there was again war at Gath, where there was a man of great stature, who had six fingers on each hand, and six toes on each foot, twenty-four in number; and he also was descended from the giants. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when he taunted Israel, Jonathan the son of Shim′e-a, David’s brother, slew him. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "These were descended from the giants in Gath; and they fell by the hand of David and by the hand of his servants."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}